# Image-creator appliance profile: a bootable USB environment whose
# sole purpose is creating working Saphira Linux images.
#
# Intentions ONLY. The package manager owns dependency closure; never
# enumerate resolved dependencies here (saphira-profiles(5)).
#
# This profile describes the appliance, never its products: the flavors
# it writes (BIOS/UEFI, openrc/systemd, saphira/saphirad, ext4/ZFS) are
# chosen in the menu at runtime. Each entry earns its place:
#
#   saphira-base        libc/loader, filesystem layout, apk, shell, core
#                       runtime, account and package tooling.
#   saphira-kernel      the kernel and its modules. Boot is impossible
#                       without it. The appliance itself boots ext4;
#                       ZFS is a creation target, never the appliance root.
#   openrc              the init system for this appliance (v0 decision).
#   grub                the bootloader, installed to the USB medium.
#   e2fsprogs           mkfs.ext4/fsck for ext4 roots, appliance and target.
#   dosfstools          mkfs.vfat. Harmless on bios-*: the creator refuses
#                       to use it there, and UEFI targets need it.
#   dialog              the menu system. No menu without it.
#   udev                the device manager: /dev/disk/by-id never
#                       exists without it (proven Egg 2026-10-19), and
#                       the menu refuses to run without persistent
#                       disk identifiers.
#   vim                 console editor for install manifests.
#   openssh             enabled at first setup with root login (v0
#                       decision): a headless appliance with no remote
#                       access is not manageable.
#   util-linux          sfdisk, wipefs, blockdev, blkid: partitioning and
#                       device handling for real-disk writes.
#   kmod                modprobe/insmod: the appliance loads the ZFS
#                       module itself before creating pools.
#   saphira-image-creator
#                       the image build engine the menu drives.
#   saphira-install-tools
#                       profiles, planner, installer and menu tooling.
#   saphira-zfs-7.2.3   ZFS kmod matching the appliance kernel: the
#                       appliance must create pools, so the module lives
#                       here, not only in its products.
#   saphira-zfs-userspace
#                       zpool/zfs binaries for pool creation.
#
# Deliberately absent, each a decision rather than an oversight:
#   - saphira-firstboot: the appliance runs firstboot's account, root
#     password and network/DNS stages ONCE as setup, then the creator
#     menu owns the console permanently;
#   - network services, firmware families, editors beyond vim: the
#     appliance creates images, it is not a server;
#   - a graphical stack of any kind (see the headless policy).
saphira-base
saphira-kernel-7.2.3
openrc
grub
e2fsprogs
dosfstools
dialog
udev
vim
openssh
util-linux
kmod
saphira-image-creator
saphira-install-tools
saphira-zfs-7.2.3
saphira-zfs-userspace
